 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S446-012\", \"clauses\": {\"multiply_numbers\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"What is {a} × {b}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F16 is a question_text family whose a and b slots multiply two generated numbers, so it asks the learner to multiply numbers directly.\"}, \"6_7_8_and_9_multiplication_tables\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"What is {a} × {b}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F16's a slot prints 6 to 9 (key a, printed_runs \\\"6 to 9\\\"), so its problems are drawn from the 6, 7, 8 and 9 tables. F04 names the tables in a hint but is not a question.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F03\", \"F05\", \"F17\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Think of it as {b} {count_noun}: {groups}.\", \"We need to {mul_phrase} {b} {count_noun}.\", \"{a} × {b} = {fill_value}\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F03 (hint) prints {b} with printed_runs \\\"1 to 5\\\" and {count_noun} from the group phrases, which have both singular and plural members, with derived_from_values a and b. The packet does not bind the singular to b = 1, so a value of b above 1 can pair with a singular phrase, and b = 1 can pair with a plural phrase, both producing ungrammatical or miscounted hint text. The groups slot draws from families F07 to F10, which print 1, 2, 4 and 5 addends. No family prints three addends, yet b can be 3, so a three-group hint can print a wrong number of addends. F05 (hint) has the same count_noun pairing gap across b values 1 to 9. F17 (format_data.statement, nested in F18) has a fill_value distractor domain with 20 fixed members and no derived_from_values. Those members include values that equal a × b for some a in 6 to 9 and b in 1 to 4 or 6 to 9, so a distractor can make the statement true while it is keyed as a false statement. The packet does not show the generator excluding the true product from the distractors. F18's own template is sound, but it prints the F17 statement as a True or False question. F14 and F15 keep the T/F answer and statements within the multiplication facts and the vocabulary gate, with 'missing number' in cumulative_vocab. F19 and F20 use 'array', which is absent from both cumulative_vocab and NOT_YET_KNOWN, and F20 instructs the learner to shade squares, which only makes sense if the item is an interactive drawing. Neither is named as a failure because the packet does not settle the vocabulary gate or the interaction mode.\"}",
